      "message": "crypto: cleanse HMAC hasher state on destruction\n\nCHMAC_SHA256 and CHMAC_SHA512 do not cleanse their two hasher objects\nwhen they are destroyed. After Finalize(), the outer hasher's state\nholds the HMAC output, and the inner hasher's buffer still holds the\nlast bytes of the message. For CExtKey::SetSeed() these are the master\nkey and the seed. For BIP32Hash() on a hardened child, they are the\nchild key tweak and the parent private key.\n\nAdd destructors that cleanse both hashers with memory_cleanse(), as\nthe ChaCha20 classes do. This completes the cleansing of rkey and temp\ndone in the same files by #35254.",
